# Vault conventions

This repo is an Obsidian vault plus agent workflows. Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root for the full map before doing multi-file work.

- Keep the numbered-folder structure (`00_Inbox` through `11_Agents`). New unsorted notes go to `00_Inbox/`.
- Preserve YAML frontmatter on every note you edit. New notes get frontmatter matching the templates in `_templates/`.
- Link related notes with `[[wikilinks]]`, not bare paths.
- Never delete vault notes. Move strays to `00_Inbox/` if their home is unclear.
- Skills live in `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with `name` and `description` frontmatter. Skill outputs go to `Daily-Briefs/` unless the skill says otherwise.
- Never commit zips, videos, or other large binaries. They are gitignored on purpose.
- Approval tiers: reading, analyzing, drafting, and building files is autonomous. Anything outbound (sending email, posting to Slack, deploying a site, spending money) requires explicit approval from Dillon first.
